W: 1 Christ, whose glory fills the skies,
W: Christ, the true and only Light,
W: Sun of righteousness, arise,
W: triumph o&apos;er the shade of night;
W: Day-spring from on high, be near;
W: Day-star, in my heart appear.
W:
W: 2 Dark and cheerless is the morn
W: unaccompanied by Thee;
W: joyless is the day&apos;s return,
W: till Thy mercy&apos;s beams I see,
W: till they inward light impart,
W: glad my eyes, and warm my heart.
W:
W: 3 Visit then this soul of mine,
W: pierce the gloom of sin and grief;
W: fill me, radiancy divine,
W: scatter all my unbelief;
W: more and more Thyself display,
W: shining to the perfect day.</miscellaneous-field>
